  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_a0d9fdd40b64498a99cca9ed0acc0ec4",
      "statement": "The framework's settings object is built at import time: `sincpro_conf.settings` is the result of `build_config_obj(DefaultFrameworkConfig, DEFAULT_CONFIG_FILE_PATH)` executed at module scope, and because `sincpro_framework/__init__.py` imports the logger and the bus, importing the package is enough to trigger it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/__init__.py#L1-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:10270fe191adede4abc73e4d73de98f1257589283e004ebef28a7126e7b49da7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/sincpro_conf.py#L124-L124",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5e2537d075dcac7cf3f1255961058cee32f1e3d7ced0e718fc0d0a98f3201860:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3c77086049bb4ed695f9870853d2d7b8",
      "statement": "The configuration file path is resolved once at import time from `SINCPRO_FRAMEWORK_CONFIG_FILE` when set and non-empty, otherwise from the packaged `conf/sincpro_framework_conf.yml`, so setting the override variable after the package has been imported has no effect.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L1258-L1262",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:16b643ea4a74ca79364951e18991bd6e32912d7816d6c11fb67f05c2c0e4f837:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/sincpro_conf.py#L10-L13",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7cc4693a2ca66ccf8cf629e2e7b2a122d425d4fc640ea25e5c146f84c3e56220:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_df9e56a594c544efb1fb4860ebd68607",
      "statement": "The shipped conf file assigns every field to a `$ENV:` reference rather than a literal, so all effective defaults live in the Python model `DefaultFrameworkConfig`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/conf/sincpro_framework_conf.yml#L1-L9",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a086952ccd6535c0dafc08a7bf704e71f2d8d4391fd19b2554461859a957d8e1:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/sincpro_conf.py#L90-L101",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2d655a35af35bdeab95bc4b49a4713853745a37e39c2125a8231442e66e15b56:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_169b0e44e7cb447aa84325cfd6600f33",
      "statement": "`SincproConfig` resolves `$ENV:` references through a single Pydantic `model_validator(mode=\"before\")` that rewrites string values whose prefix is `$ENV:`, reading the name after the prefix with `os.getenv`; non-string and nested values are left to normal submodel validation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/sincpro_conf.py#L46-L57",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7f22b241c5bc9f5bf0a7c6fef930c55413f62ddae5aaf20b099ff52cdc5f8c39:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f63016965d094e4986a2929666c95236",
      "statement": "When a referenced environment variable is set, the value is used only if `usable_env_value` accepts it for that field; otherwise the field's default is substituted and an info-level log names both the variable and the field. `usable_env_value` re-wraps the annotation with its `Field` metadata in `Annotated[...]` and validates via `TypeAdapter(...).validate_python`, returning False on any exception.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/sincpro_conf.py#L24-L38",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fa08e65126e6683865309419a481fa28a3667f038610661792f6bd665c0426f4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/sincpro_conf.py#L58-L67",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:17f6d8b758e6922eb1a19434fa65d18b97ab47056736eb5d23176f4f63f5c585:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3c61e2f5e5d74b59aaaa837693b065c5",
      "statement": "When a referenced environment variable is unset, the validator's behaviour depends on the field: a non-None default is used with an info log, a field whose default is None is set to None silently with no log, and a field with no default at all only logs — the literal `$ENV:...` text reaches Pydantic and raises `ValidationError`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/sincpro_conf.py#L68-L83",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fde23a7e6dcc7d7a906b364df2a72247983033a540e987aef56b8357c7e8b68a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/config/test_env_variables.py#L61-L105",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:205fc71fcb1f5c0775d451fc3af9fcd0669c987ec872a6124fabea1918cb7ddf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b82773599aad408da3e48ec05859b182",
      "statement": "The type check on an environment value exists because `settings` is constructed during import: the documented invariant is that a malformed deployment variable must not raise before the framework is importable, so an unusable optional value degrades to its default instead of aborting the import — the case of `otlp_traces_sample_rate` fed by `OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG`, where out-of-range or non-numeric values fall back to 1.0.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/sincpro_conf.py#L24-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cf7175726071c8e1171a9414288ee15bfaa36540efd2ac445144a12b03d5e76a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/sincpro_conf.py#L97-L97",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f408e0288163de162c7642a9867095ff6c8843b1bed69e479af132717ed10543:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/config/test_env_variables.py#L107-L147",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1a1d6595c1d8a65f993b7968169aee7a003b3ff8bda541c32c74bd8778df0ed2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4b8c648b93284284b7a35336a1bacf98",
      "statement": "`build_config_obj(class_config_obj, config_path, sub_key=None)` loads the YAML with `yaml.safe_load`, replaces the mapping with the named section when `sub_key` is given (raising `ValueError` naming the missing section and the file otherwise), prints a `read yaml file ... for config <ClassName>` line to stdout via `print`, and then constructs the model class from the mapping.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/sincpro_conf.py#L104-L121",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2cfcf8a1d11d9b97b75a0adfa5f69fc3295eec9a15872cbe7d91d56de8d62c62:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/sincpro_conf.py#L18-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8c2270d7e2fa063c4118078f9e8f7ce1e40c5f443131edb3ee5a81dc12b70db2:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/config/test_config_obj.py#L44-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e135cffa3be0ac7a8bfcdfba0ce2c5bfc7b05f40d087eed7c82913546a7c72fa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c15e21b241a44c63a9b4266486f925d5",
      "statement": "`DefaultFrameworkConfig` declares nine fields with their defaults and both resolvers: the log level (`Literal[\"INFO\", \"DEBUG\"]`, default `\"DEBUG\"`), log backend (`Literal[\"print\", \"stdlib\", \"file\"]`, default `\"print\"`), log file path (None), and the optional observability fields `otlp_endpoint`, `otlp_traces_sample_rate` (bounded 0.0-1.0, default 1.0), `sentry_dsn`, `app_release`, `otel_service_name` and `tenant`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/sincpro_conf.py#L90-L101",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2d655a35af35bdeab95bc4b49a4713853745a37e39c2125a8231442e66e15b56:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_29e3294bdab24bfda52f7ca4ffa9a0cb",
      "statement": "Global logging is configured from `settings` at import time of `sincpro_logger.py`, passing the log level, backend and file path into `configure_global_logging`, so an assignment into `settings` after import neither reconfigures logging nor is the supported way to change it — the environment is.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L1251-L1251",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b710bc230d5a3e624f440a477ff40b0a98e705ef44d0f1c3b4d8631d48391846:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/sincpro_logger.py#L5-L11",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9ecea4c9dcd6c4307e9ce6b5c1162d31aa8a36546b99cdd75f8a4fa42335a645:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a73d557467944337b3f37b4817b2153b",
      "statement": "`is_logger_in_debug()` tests the `sincpro_framework_log_level` settings field rather than the logger's effective level, and the feature and application-service buses use it (alongside their own `log_after_execution` flag) to decide whether to emit the pre-execution info line, so with the default DEBUG that line is on.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/bus.py#L104-L104",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:075d2cdba8a848fb1b86e47051e87fb5632235e96dd15c6141605cc65506eb00:"
